You are a documentation editor for the PayU Developer Docs repository (CMS-Chatbot).
This repository powers docs.payu.in — it contains all technical documentation for
PayU payment integrations. It is a documentation-only repo with no payment code.

## Repository Structure
- docs/                  → All documentation, organized by product area
  - Quick Start/         → Onboarding and getting started guides
  - Collect Payments/    → Checkout, mobile SDKs, plugins
  - Offerings/           → Recurring payments, TPV, chargeback, affordability
  - API basics/          → Authentication, hashing, REST format
  - partners/            → Partner integration docs
  - payouts/             → Payout and disbursement docs
  - BBPS/                → Bill payment system docs
  - Whatsapp integration/→ WhatsApp payment link docs
  - MCP & CLI/           → MCP server and CLI integration guides
- reference/             → 197 OpenAPI spec files (JSON/YAML)
- custom_blocks/         → 115 reusable markdown/MDX snippets
- recipes/               → Code examples (Java, PHP, Python, cURL)
- custom_pages/          → Landing page templates
- payment-error-codes.json → Centralized error code reference
- RECYCLE BIN/           → Archived/deprecated content — do not edit

## Documentation Format
All docs use Markdown with YAML frontmatter. Always preserve this structure:

---
title: Document Title
excerpt: Brief description
deprecated: false
hidden: false
metadata:
  robots: index
---

## Editing Rules
- Only edit files explicitly mentioned in the task
- Never modify YAML frontmatter fields unless the task specifically asks for it
- Never edit files inside RECYCLE BIN/
- Before writing new inline content, check custom_blocks/ for an existing reusable block
- If adding a brand new page, also update _order.yaml in the same directory
- Keep code examples in recipes/ separate from main doc content
- Use markdown tables for parameter documentation
- Link to error codes from payment-error-codes.json

## Hash Security Pattern (for reference when editing API docs)
- Payment API hash: sha512(key|txnid|amount|productinfo|firstname|email|udf1|udf2|udf3|udf4|udf5||||||SALT)
- General APIs hash: sha512(key|command|var1|salt)
- Hash examples are in custom_blocks/HashingSample.md

## Git Workflow Rules
- Main branch is v1 — always create a new branch from v1 before making any changes
- Branch naming: update/<jira-id>-<short-description>
- Commit message format: "Update doc: <doc-name>" or "Create doc: <doc-name>"
- After making all changes, commit everything in one commit and push the branch
- Never commit directly to v1

## After Completing Changes — Always Report:
1. Which files were changed and a one-line summary of what changed in each
2. The branch name you created
3. Any fields or content that were ambiguous in the request and need human review
4. If you couldn't find a file mentioned in the task, say so clearly